## MCP – Telegram (Kiro) vs rest (mcp-cli)

**Telegram is the only MCP attached to your Kiro session.** Use the Telegram MCP tools directly (no mcp-cli for Telegram):

| Telegram MCP tools (use directly in Kiro) |
|-------------------------------------------|
| `send_msg_to_default_group` – send report or message to default group |
| `get_default_group_messages` – read recent messages (e.g. `{"limit":20}`) |
| `send_approval_request` – send draft for approval with buttons |
| `get_approval_responses` – poll for user Approve/Reject |
| `finalize_approval` – after acting, finalize with `chat_id`, `message_id`, `selected_text` |

**Approval (sensitive actions):** use the Telegram MCP tool `send_approval_request` with `{"text":"...", "keyboard":[[{"text":"✅ Approve","callback_data":"approve_1"},{"text":"❌ Reject","callback_data":"reject_1"}]]}`. Then poll `get_approval_responses`, execute or discard, then `finalize_approval`.

**Everything else (WhatsApp, Discord, Gmail, Jira)** – use mcp-cli: `mcp-cli call <server> <tool> '<json>'`. List tools: `mcp-cli info <server>`.

| Server (mcp-cli) | Tools you need |
|------------------|-----------------|
| **whatsapp** | `list_messages`, `list_chats`, `search_contacts`, `send_message`, `get_message_context` |
| **discord-mcp** | `discord_get_dms`, `discord_send_dm`, `discord_send_group_message` |
| **gmail** | `gmail_list_emails`, `gmail_search_emails`, `gmail_send_email` |
| **mcp-atlassian** | Jira: `jira_get_issue`, `jira_search`, etc. |

